{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_mailboxes_mailbox", "label": "Mailbox", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Exactly one queue per actor is what makes the one-message-at-a-time guarantee physically true.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/fundamentals/mailboxes.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_mailboxes_unbounded_fifo_default", "label": "Unbounded FIFO als Default", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "The bounded default of v0.10\u2013v0.15 failed twice over: the ceiling never existed because system messages were never capped, and a mailbox cannot know what it discards \u2014 drop-head silently dropped Terminated signals and delivery acknowledgments.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/fundamentals/mailboxes.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_mailboxes_boundedmailbox", "label": "BoundedMailbox", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Constructing one directly defaults to reject because nothing can be assumed about what is expendable, while withMailboxOverflow defaults to drop-head, the policy matching the workloads people actually bound.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/fundamentals/mailboxes.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_mailboxes_prioritymailbox", "label": "PriorityMailbox", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "priorityFor runs at enqueue time, lower numbers first, ties broken FIFO; it breaks send order across kinds, so invariants that depend on arrival order need two actors and a router instead.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/fundamentals/mailboxes.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_mailboxes_overflow_policies", "label": "Overflow-Policies (drop-head / drop-new / reject)", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "A backpressure-versus-loss trade-off: fresh-wins for telemetry, first-wins for command streams, reject when the sender has a meaningful backoff answer.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/fundamentals/mailboxes.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_mailboxes_priority_overflow_policies", "label": "Priority-Overflow-Policies (drop-lowest-priority)", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "drop-head is deliberately absent: on a priority queue the head is the message priorityFor called most important, so dropping it would defeat the reason for choosing that mailbox.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/fundamentals/mailboxes.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_mailboxes_system_message_precedence", "label": "Vorrang von System-Nachrichten", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "System messages jump the whole user queue so a supervisor decision takes effect at once; ref.stop() does not, because it is a user message (PoisonPill) and drains first.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/fundamentals/mailboxes.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_mailboxes_ringbuffer", "label": "RingBuffer als Queue-Unterbau", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "A queue without a ceiling has to stay cheap when it gets deep: dequeuing advances an index instead of reindexing everything behind it, so delivery cost does not grow with the backlog.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/fundamentals/mailboxes.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_mailboxes_withmailbox", "label": "withMailbox(factory)", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Replaces the queue rather than configuring it, so combining it with withMailboxCapacity is a configuration error instead of a silent precedence rule.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/fundamentals/mailboxes.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_mailboxes_withmailboxcapacity", "label": "withMailboxCapacity / withMailboxOverflow", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Capacity is what creates the bound; a policy without a capacity is rejected rather than silently ignored, because an unbounded mailbox never overflows.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/fundamentals/mailboxes.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_mailboxes_dropreportingmailbox", "label": "DropReportingMailbox", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Registration is additive, so a custom onDrop keeps firing beside the stock counter.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/fundamentals/mailboxes.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_mailboxes_mailboxfullerror", "label": "MailboxFullError", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "reject throws at the tell call site, so B's full mailbox surfaces as A restarting repeatedly \u2014 wire a metric on droppedCount rather than reading supervisor logs.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/fundamentals/mailboxes.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_mailboxes_stash_reinsert", "label": "Stash-Wiedereinspielen \u00fcber prependUser", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "PriorityMailbox re-runs the priority function instead of prepending, so unstashAll goes through enqueue and a bounded priority mailbox can drop while replaying; BoundedMailbox's unstash path bypasses the bound.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/fundamentals/mailboxes.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_mailboxes_drop_metrics", "label": "actor_mailbox_dropped_total", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Labelled per class, not per actor: shedding is what a bounded mailbox is for, so a per-actor label would create a permanent series for every actor behaving exactly as designed.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/fundamentals/mailboxes.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_mailboxes_shared_mailbox_antipattern", "label": "Geteilte Mailbox-Instanz (Antipattern)", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Returning the same instance from two factories pipes both actors' messages into one queue \u2014 the factory exists so each actor gets a fresh one.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/fundamentals/mailboxes.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_mailboxes_mailbox", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_mailboxes_unbounded_fifo_default", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/fundamentals/mailboxes.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_mailboxes_boundedmailbox", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_mailboxes_mailbox", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.95, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/fundamentals/mailboxes.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_mailboxes_prioritymailbox", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_mailboxes_mailbox", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.95, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/fundamentals/mailboxes.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_mailboxes_overflow_policies", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_mailboxes_boundedmailbox", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/fundamentals/mailboxes.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_mailboxes_priority_overflow_policies", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_mailboxes_prioritymailbox", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/fundamentals/mailboxes.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_mailboxes_priority_overflow_policies", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_mailboxes_overflow_policies", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/fundamentals/mailboxes.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_mailboxes_mailboxfullerror", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_mailboxes_overflow_policies", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/fundamentals/mailboxes.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_mailboxes_ringbuffer", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_mailboxes_unbounded_fifo_default", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/fundamentals/mailboxes.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_mailboxes_withmailbox", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_mailboxes_mailbox", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/fundamentals/mailboxes.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_mailboxes_withmailboxcapacity", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_mailboxes_overflow_policies", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/fundamentals/mailboxes.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_mailboxes_dropreportingmailbox", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_mailboxes_drop_metrics", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/fundamentals/mailboxes.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_mailboxes_stash_reinsert", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_mailboxes_prioritymailbox", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/fundamentals/mailboxes.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_mailboxes_shared_mailbox_antipattern", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_fundamentals_mailboxes_withmailbox", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/fundamentals/mailboxes.mdx", "source_location": null